## Cursor Automations (Super-Agent)

When discussing or managing **Cursor Automations**, apply **Cursor Automations Operating Model** in `docs/ops/cursor-operating-model.md` (including **Plan and Budget Gate**).

- **Never** recommend paid Cursor plan upgrades, paid overages, usage-based automation, or paid add-ons **by default** — only if the user explicitly asks about paid options.
- For Automations: first confirm **current-plan availability** and **no-extra-cost** constraint; ask the user or inspect Cursor settings when possible.
- If Automations are **unavailable**, recommend the **manual daily Super-Agent workflow** (same outputs: health, memory freshness, security drift, next batch, approval phrase; no implementation without approval).
- Prefer **daily read-only** automations first (when free and available); **PR-only** only after read-only mode proves reliable.
- Automations must be **managed by the Super-Agent** and **periodically reviewed** (weekly rules review).
- Never let automations bypass **Sensitive Batch Gate**, **Memory Update Protocol**, **Final Evidence Pack**, or **explicit approval** (`APPROVED TO IMPLEMENT: <batch-name>` when gated).
- Automations may recommend strongly but must **not** treat recommendations as authorization.

## Docs-only batches

Do not change runtime, Prisma schema, APIs, UI, tests, or dependencies unless explicitly requested.
